{"id":"noopept","name":"Noopept","form":"capsule","status":"Documented","aliases":"","category":"Nootropic","summarySources":"TripSit","summary":"A common nootropic often attributed with temporarily increasing intelligence, concentration, focus, and memory recall. Daily use is reported to create dependency with withdrawls reportedly causing negative cognitive effects and ability. The nootropic is often taken in combinations or 'stacks' with other nootropics.","advisory":"Avoid: Due to noopept modulating AMPA and NMDA receptors, dissociative drugs such as ketamine will have diminished effects. The drug is reported to have unpredictable potentiating effects on drugs such as alcohol, cannabis, psychedelics, and stimulants. Caution is advised when mixing.","doseMaxTick":30,"doseUnit":"mg","doseRows":[{"roa":"Oral","source":"TripSit","unit":"mg","light":"5 mg","common":"10 mg","strong":"10–20 mg+","heavy":"20 mg+","commonEstimate":10,"band":{"low":10,"high":10},"domain":[4,27],"segments":{"light":[5,5],"common":[10,10],"strong":[10,20],"heavy":[20,25.92]}},{"roa":"Sublingual","source":"TripSit","unit":"mg","light":"2–5 mg","common":"5–10 mg","strong":"10 mg+","heavy":"10 mg+","commonEstimate":8,"band":{"low":5,"high":10},"domain":[1.6,22],"segments":{"light":[2,5],"common":[5,10],"strong":[10,10],"heavy":[10,21.12]}},{"roa":"Insufflated","source":"TripSit","unit":"mg","light":"2–5 mg","common":"5–10 mg","strong":"10 mg+","heavy":"10 mg+","commonEstimate":8,"band":{"low":5,"high":10},"domain":[1.6,22],"segments":{"light":[2,5],"common":[5,10],"strong":[10,10],"heavy":[10,21.12]}}],"durationSources":"TripSit","durationRows":[{"roa":"Oral","onset":"15–30 min","comeup":"—","peak":"—","offset":"—","afterEffects":"1–8 h","total":"3–6 h"},{"roa":"Sublingual","onset":"5–10 min","comeup":"—","peak":"—","offset":"—","afterEffects":"1–8 h","total":"3–6 h"},{"roa":"Insufflated","onset":"0–5 min","comeup":"—","peak":"—","offset":"—","afterEffects":"1–8 h","total":"3–6 h"},{"roa":"General","onset":"—","comeup":"—","peak":"—","offset":"—","afterEffects":"1–8 h","total":"3–6 h"}],"subjectiveEffects":[{"name":"Acuity enhancement","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Acuity_enhancement"},{"name":"Anxiety suppression","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Anxiety_suppression"},{"name":"Colour enhancement","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Colour_enhancement"},{"name":"Focus enhancement","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Focus_enhancement"},{"name":"Irritability","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Irritability"},{"name":"Memory enhancement","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Memory_enhancement"},{"name":"Motivation enhancement","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Motivation_enhancement"},{"name":"Rejuvenation","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Rejuvenation"},{"name":"Spontaneous tactile sensations","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Spontaneous_tactile_sensations"},{"name":"Stimulation","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Stimulation"},{"name":"Thought acceleration","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Thought_acceleration"},{"name":"Thought connectivity","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Thought_connectivity"},{"name":"Wakefulness","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Wakefulness"}],"combinations":[],"citations":[],"helpfulLinks":[{"title":"TripSit Factsheet","description":"Rapid harm-reduction summary and combination data","url":"https://drugs.tripsit.me/noopept"},{"title":"Erowid Experience Vaults","description":"First-person experience reports and archives","url":"https://www.erowid.org/experiences/subs/exp_Noopept_.shtml"},{"title":"Wikipedia","description":"Encyclopedia article","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Omberacetam"},{"title":"Wikidata","description":"Structured data on Noopept","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q7049784"},{"title":"維基百科","description":"zh:Encyclopedia article","url":"https://zh.wikipedia.org/zh-tw/%E6%98%82%E8%B4%9D%E8%A5%BF%E5%9D%A6"}],"wikidata":"Q7049784","formula":"C17H22N2O4","molarMass":318.4,"pharmacology":{"text":"One oft-cited study (originally published in Russian) conducted on rats, suggests that Noopept works via the \"antioxidant effect, the anti-inflammatory action, and the ability to inhibit the neurotoxicity of excess calcium and glutamate, and to improve the blood rheology\". Studies in rats suggest, Noopept is a prodrug of the endogenous dipeptide cycloprolylglycine.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"Omberacetam","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Omberacetam#Pharmacology"},"uses":{"text":"It has been evaluated for neuroprotective effects in treating brain injuries and stroke.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"Omberacetam","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Omberacetam"},"zh":"昂貝西坦","zhOther":"奧貝拉西坦","summaryZh":"昂貝西坦，又稱N-苯乙醯-l-脯氨醯甘氨酸乙酯，被宣傳為一種益智藥，是環甘氨酸-脯氨酸的前體藥物。其他名稱包括商品名Noopept（俄語：Ноопепт）。"}